<p>Okay, wow… you weren't kidding when you said wordy, were you?</p>
<p>Okay, three things.</p>
<p>One, paragraphs. Seriously, blocks of text are inordinately hard on the eyes, and decrease interest in reading something. Try and sort that out.</p>
<p>Two, formatting. It always looks better when you bold titles, put speech sections in quote boxes, and put little quotes in italics. It makes them stand out, and again, easier to read.</p>
<p>Three, if you've got support documents that long, you might want to put them into a separate document <a href="/incident-reports-eye-witness-interviews-and-personal-logs">here</a>, simply for simplification and the sake of clarity.</p>
<p>Other than that, the idea seems sound. It's just your formatting skills need work, and maybe being a little more impartial in your writing.</p>

