<p>Kulzn- Mr. Name, tear down this wall of text? well I'm not going to tear it down, but i did divide it up a little. Hopefully it's a little better on the east germ- i mean eyes.</p>
<p>scratskinner- well its a ticket to the never ending rides, but my original idea was to have it apply to a lot of things, like fundraiser dinners, amusement parks, theaters, that type of thing but i decided it didn't really work. However I did have a last document where an intern was just walking around with the ticket (because they have forbidden experimentation, but she still wanted see how it changed from form to form, she was interested.) and then all of a sudden for some reason it starting changing to every place that used tickets, extremely rapidly, like never before. They thought either that it was suddenly doing this because the force behind the ticket wanted to destroy them or desperately desired to communicate with them, so out of all the locations that were offered they choose a movie theater, because it was the only one with semi automated visual and audio capabilities. Of course the film shown drove everyone insane. oh and the title box outside said SCP-342 playing forever *rolls eyes* i cut this because it seemed like i was making the ticket a little too sentient.</p>
<p>i also had the idea that near the end, the ticket would start appearing in the researcher's pockets when they were on leave, and they would hand it over without looking, absentmindedly, and get trapped, like it was hunting them down.</p>
<p>*sees ticket getting ripped*</p>
<p>Dr. Haber: oh my god what have i done</p>
<p>that sort of thing.</p>
<p>I'm not going to use either of these ideas, but if someone wants to put them down, feel free. i just ask that they put them in a separate linked page, i kinda want to keep this article in its original form. (that idea seems to be going against the general opinion so far that its needs to be changed immediately because it's filled with suck)</p>
<p>p.s I think I'm going to start out all my new pages with <sup>^</sup><sup>^</sup><sup>^</sup><sup>^</sup>^^^^, so it looks like barbed wire fencing. the Berlin SCP! and maybe i can make a sniper out of symbols, although that seems like it would be a little trickier.</p>

